    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** (82.70) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) headline our lineup as the premier starts. **Kyle Tucker** is in a prime position to capitalize on a favorable matchup against Lowder; his 19% SP skill advantage combined with his consistent high-floor production makes him the anchor of our outfield. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned for a breakout night against Ober. While the base projection for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** was moderate, the combination of Ober\u2019s 4.77 xERA and a positive park factor pushes his efficiency score well into the elite tier, making him a must-start at MI. **Heliot Ramos** (67.76) rounds out our top-tier plays, specifically benefitting from his elite sprint speed against a slow pitcher delivery, which provides a unique boost to our stolen base ceiling in a category where every marginal gain is vital.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision was leaving **Miguel Vargas** (52.14) on the bench. He was the strongest performer among the reserves, narrowly missing the cut behind **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.46) and **Josh Jung** (59.90). While **Miguel Vargas** offers solid xwOBA metrics, the optimizer favored the higher platoon-adjusted upside and order positioning of our starters. We are closely monitoring the risk profile of **Gunnar Henderson** (51.14); while he remains in the lineup, his score is currently dampened by a significant 15% penalty due to a challenging platoon matchup against Manaea. Owners should note that while our floor remains stable, the risk of a sub-50 performance from **Sam Antonacci** (41.45) is elevated due to his L/L matchup against Griffin, but we are holding him in the lineup tonight to balance our roster distribution.",
